# Docs markdown style

When writing or editing files under `docs/`:

- Do not use `**...**` (or `__...__`) for bold emphasis. Prefer plain prose, headings, or backticks for code/identifiers.
- Do not use em dashes (—) or en dashes (–). Use a colon, comma, parentheses, or a period instead.

Examples:

```markdown
<!-- Bad -->
- **News (`postType: news`)** — external hub cards only.

<!-- Good -->
- News (`postType: news`): external hub cards only.
```
